Inline state bucket creation and default it to dev-genai-cloudrag

Replace the tf-init composite action with plain AWS CLI steps in the workflow
itself, and delete .github/actions entirely. Bucket creation still runs before
every terraform init, now as an explicit step in each job rather than a shared
action.

TF_STATE_BUCKET defaults to dev-genai-cloudrag, so no repository variable is
needed; setting the variable still overrides it for another account or fork.

bootstrap performs the full setup, including versioning, SSE, a public access
block and a policy denying non-TLS requests, because Terraform state stores
secrets in plaintext. The three Terraform jobs keep a shorter create-if-absent
guard so they remain correct when re-run individually.
